course: dictionary
lesson: 12860
title: Engulf: covered completely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To engulf something is to cover it completely, or surround it so that you cannot see past it. Water, flames, fog and fear can all engulf things. Look at the clues: «The flood engulfed the village in just one hour.» The village was covered by water, so engulfed means covered completely.
explain: Engulf can also describe a feeling. «Panic engulfed him when he lost his way.» Panic cannot be touched, but it can fill a person completely. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Panic covered him completely" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Engulf is a verb, so it changes its form: engulf, engulfs, engulfed, engulfing. «Smoke engulfs the room» is happening now. «Smoke engulfed the room» happened in the past. Ask yourself what is being covered or swallowed, and the meaning will follow.
fact: Engulf means to cover or surround something completely.
fact: «Engulfed» is the past tense: «The fire engulfed the barn.»
fact: «Engulfed in flames» means completely surrounded by fire.
fact: Scientists say a white blood cell can engulf a germ, taking it in so that it can be destroyed.
fact: When a feeling engulfs you, it fills you up completely, as in «engulfed by fear».
exercise: «The flood engulfed the village in just one hour.» What does engulfed mean here? | Sung to | *Covered completely | Dried out | Lightly tapped
exercise: «Panic engulfed him when he lost his way.» What does engulfed mean here? | Showed him the way home | *Filled him completely | Made him laugh | Left him alone for a moment
exercise: Which form of engulf is the past tense? | engulfing | engulf | *engulfed | engulfs
test: «The sandstorm engulfed the road.» What does engulfed mean? | *Covered and hidden completely | Swept clean | Cracked open | Lit up brightly
test: Which phrase means completely surrounded by fire? | barely a spark | gently glowing | *engulfed in flames | drooped low
exam: A white blood cell engulfs a germ. What happens to the germ? | It turns into a blood cell | It becomes stronger | It runs away | *It is swallowed up and destroyed
